pec section 15's proposed\n71-layout) are NOT created. Instead:\n72-\n73:- `runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py` (top-level, owned by N31) is the one\n74-  targeted-repair engine, used by both unit (D17-D21) and workbook (D29,\n75-  D31) repair.\n76:- `runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py` (top-level, owned by N31) is the\n77:  one denominator-reduction/acceptance engine, used by both D16/D22/D23\n78-  (unit) and D28 (workbook).\n79:- `runtime/langgraph_factory/workbook.py` (top-level, owned by N32) is the\n80:  workbook assembly/coverage/release engine (D24, D25, D26, D27, D29, D31,\n81-  D32) plus the two product-terminal call sites.\n82-- `nodes/` (owned by N22) contains exactly: `inputs.py`, `sources.py`,\n83-  `domain.py`, `content.py`, `visuals.py`, `render.py`, `review.py`,\n--\n93-`writes` set names it. Resolution: `RuntimeContext` construction (opening\n94-services: path guards, evidence writer, subprocess transport registry,\n95-source retriever, signal token, clock) is implemented as a factory function\n96:inside `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py`, owned by N20. No standalone\n97-`context.py` file is created. `RuntimeContext` the *type* (a frozen\n98-dataclass, not checkpointed) lives in `state.py` per spec section 5.1,\n99-owned by N11.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
