ly real conditional-edge destinations (evidence/guard_destinations_no_accept_route.txt) are failure/interrupt/terminal-write — there is no route by which a cleanly-reviewed unit is ever accepted. `repair.py`/`acceptance.py` (N31's modules) are fully implemented and function-level-tested but never registered into `StateGraph` by any node. N31's own result record (`results/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE.result.v1.md`) explicitly disclosed this as unfinished (\"Neither module is registered into the compiled graph yet... N32's write\") yet still recorded `status: PASSED`; N32 did not close it (see F2) and no subsequent node routed a rework edge for it — it silently reached N90 unresolved.\n  Fingerprint: `binding_inventory()` excludes D16-D23; `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` rows 2-7 (owner `N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE`) remain open against `sha256(unit_graph.py)=286995f3...`.\n\n- **F2 — workbook engine (D24-D32) unreachable from the compiled production graph, and N32's own result record misrepresents its shipped artifact.**\n  Owner: `N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS`. Rework key: `workbook_or_terminal`.\n  Evidence: `register_workbook_topology()` (graph.py:456) is fully implemented and adds/wires D24-D32 correctly **when called directly** (as `test_plan26_workbook.py:772` does against a private builder) — but it is never called from `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` (evidence/register_workbook_topology_grep.txt: its only two call sites outside its own definition are both inside `test_plan26_workbook.py`). `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` row 1 (owner `N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS`) — `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT`'s `manifest_exhausted` guard value naming `D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE` — remains open; D24-D32 are entirely absent from the 34 compiled production nodes (evidence/compiled_graph_nodes.txt). This directly contradicts `results/N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS.result.v1.md`'s own narrative text, which states verbatim: *\"`register_workbook_topology()` (new, called by `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` right after `register_skeleton()`)\"* — that claim is false against the actual receipted artifact: `graph.py`'s receipted hash (`eae00c21...`, `results/v3/N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS.receipt.v1.json` → `outputs`) is byte-identical to the file live in this repo today, and that file does not contain the claimed call. (N32's own result record separately, and correctly, discloses the narrower \"D24 not reachable from D05\" gap later in the same document — the two passages are internally inconsistent with each other, and the more optimistic one is the one that is wrong.) N40 inherited this hash unchanged and independently, accurately described the same gap (\"a live run that reaches an unwired destination raises `KeyError`\"); N50 did not re-verify graph reachability at the compiled-graph level (its `test_no_second_production_factory` checks for a *second* path, not for *completeness* of the one path) and did not route a rework edge for it either.\n  Fingerprint: `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` (graph.py:488-509) does not call `register_workbook_topology`; `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` row 1 (owner `N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS`) remains open against `sha256(graph.py)=eae00c21...`.\n\n- **F3 (non-blocking, informational) — N60's `NOT_AVAILABLE` is a genuine, reproduced external-credential gap, not an implementation defect.** No owner/rework edge; not routed. Confirmed independently by this audit reading N60's own commands/evidence and cross-checking that `runtime/run_curriculum.py`'s hash (`76da9110...`) is unchanged since N50, so the blocker is not a regression introduced after N50. Recorded here only because Test 7 above depends on this determination.\n\n## Invalidated descendants\n\nPer LOOP, F1 and F2 each invalidate their owning node and every descendant reachable from it in `implementation.graph.v3.yaml`'s edge list:\n- F1 invalidates `N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE -> N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS -> N40_CLI_CUTOVER -> N50_ADVERSARIAL_REGRESSION -> {N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF, N90_FINAL_AUDIT}`.\n- F2 invalidates `N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS -> N40_CLI_CUTOVER -> N50_ADVERSARIAL_REGRESSION -> {N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF, N90_FINAL_AUDIT}` (subsumed by F1's wider invalidation since N32 is downstream of N31).\n- This is the first traversal of both `repair_or_unit_acceptance` and `workbook_or_terminal` as N90-initiated rework edges (no prior `results/N90_FINAL_AUDIT.result.v1.md` or `results/v3/logs/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/` entries existed before this run) — not a second or third occurrence, so `BLOCKED` here reflects this audit's own verdict per the node's TEST/LOOP contract (an unresolved blocking finding), not a loop-exhaustion case. The runner should resume graph scheduling at `N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE` and return to a fresh N90 audit once F1 and F2 are closed and re-verified at the compiled-graph level (i.e., by executing `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` and asserting D16-D32 are members of `compiled.get_graph().nodes`, and that a real `unit_denominator_passed` / `manifest_exhausted` routing decision reaches them — not by re-reading N31/N32's prose).\n\n## Hashes\n\n| Path | sha256 |\n|---|---|\n| plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/spec/langgraph_curriculum_factory.spec.v1.md | 44e63e6271cae25f14f0bc970c598d1c15da41b67ae3cdf811bbb2f2303536e6 |\n| plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/implementation.graph.v3.yaml | 3c4177f9a239279b86e1a912a0b704e3b7867693fcb4b98fe00c73c33caee867 |\n| plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/N50_ADVERSARIAL_REGRESSION.result.v1.md | 796e197370e486990f5d47636c8c714bbf62b5422de1bbad03cec72d546cfe7d |\n| plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF.result.v1.md | 4d9e8ff47a0dc966e2fa54f71550be4ac66ed5f76f04229cabe0891ca7da2fd9 |\n| plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE.result.v1.md | 325936e48371bf40a638f97d3a5c73137775cfe44f8c8582ee6cb5e048d4224c |\n| plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS.result.v1.md | ceb509d327ccefb03d6d194ce5491279ac02a8ffa7a08574d486